config BR2_PACKAGE_VIRGILIO_BASE
	bool "virgilio-base"
	depends on BR2_USE_MMU # procd/netifd fork()
	select BR2_PACKAGE_LIBUBOX
	select BR2_PACKAGE_UBUS
	select BR2_PACKAGE_UCI
	select BR2_PACKAGE_PROCD
	select BR2_PACKAGE_UBOX
	select BR2_PACKAGE_NETIFD
	select BR2_PACKAGE_JSONFILTER
	select BR2_PACKAGE_UCODE
	help
	  Common base system shared by every Virgilio device (the OpenWrt
	  "base-files" role), independent of board and SoC:

	   - procd init scripts + rc.d layout (boot, network, system, ...
	     and the service wiring for camilladsp/statime/ptp-monitor)
	   - /etc/config defaults (system, camilladsp, inferno, statime,
	     ptp-monitor)
	   - system glue: lib/functions*.sh, rc.common, ifup/ifdown/ifstatus,
	     service, hotplug-call, login.sh, inittab, preinit
	   - ucode tools: camilladsp-genconf (uci -> camilladsp YAML/policy
	     generator) and ptp-monitor (statime usrvclock -> ubus bridge)
	   - hotplug policies and ALSA config for the inferno PCM

	  Selects the uci/procd stack it requires (procd pulls ubus and
	  udebug, netifd pulls json-c/libnl/ucode). Device-specific files
	  (network topology, board fixups, test-rig services) stay in the
	  per-board rootfs overlay.
